  "id": "Compound::DB01590 - Gene::2280",
  "verbalization": "Everolimus is implicated in the pathogenesis of neoplastic conditions through its interaction with Pimecrolimus, which binds to Fkbp1a. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways where Everolimus causes or is associated with Squamous Cell Carcinoma or Neoplasm Skin, both of which are linked to Pimecrolimus. The shared pathway involves Pimecrolimus as a mediator, with Everolimus and Pimecrolimus both classified under the broader category of Immunosuppressants and Macrolides. The integration of these pathways suggests that Everolimus may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves Pimecrolimus, which in turn interacts with Fkbp1a. The evidence points to a dependency on Pimecrolimus as a critical intermediate in the pathway, reinforcing the notion that Everolimus and Fkbp1a are connected via a mechanism involving immunosuppressive agents.",
